{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) A lower midline incision will pass through all of the followings except-", "option1": "Linea alba", "option2": "Fascia transversalis", "option3": "Pyramidalis", "option4": "Parietal peritoneum", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Abdominal_wall_layers.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"607\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Patency of the distal part of the vitellointestinal duct results in-", "option1": "Faecal fistula", "option2": "Raspberry red tumour", "option3": "Meckel's diverticulum", "option4": "Enterocystoma", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>Anomalies of the Vitello-intestinal duct:</strong></u><br /> Faecal fistula (complete patency of vitello intestinal duct)<br /> Meckel&rsquo;s diverticulum (proximal part patent)<br /> Enterocystoma (Intermediate part patent)<br /> <strong>Raspberry red tumour /cherry red tumour (Distal part patent)</strong>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) The inguinal ligament is formed by the aponeurosis of-", "option1": "External oblique", "option2": "Internal oblique", "option3": "Transversus abdominis", "option4": "Iliacus", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Inguinal_ligament_.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"898\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) The deep inguinal ring does not transmit-", "option1": "Ductus deferens", "option2": "Genital branch of genitofemoral nerve", "option3": "Round ligament of uterus", "option4": "Ilioinguinal nerve", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Inguinal_ring_contents_.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1627\" height=\"1077\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) The dartos muscle in the scrotum is derived from-", "option1": "Superficial fascia of the abdomen ", "option2": "External oblique muscle", "option3": "Internal oblique aponeurosis", "option4": "Fascia transverslis", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/scrotum_layers.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1085\" height=\"640\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which is a content of the femoral canal? ", "option1": "Femoral artery", "option2": "Femoral vein", "option3": "Femoral nerve", "option4": "Lymph node of Cloquet", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Femoral_canal_.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"936\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which is not a retroperitoneal organ? ", "option1": "Ureter", "option2": "Caecum", "option3": "Pancreas", "option4": "Descending colon", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>Retroperitoneal organs:&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Retroperitoneal_organs_LMCQ.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1416\" height=\"857\" /></strong></u>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) The epiploic foramen lies at the level of vertebra-", "option1": "T12", "option2": "L1", "option3": "L2", "option4": "L3", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Epiploic_foramen_MHS_U7hQGRu.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"582\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) The greater omentum develops from-", "option1": "Root of the mesentery", "option2": "Dorsal mesogastrium", "option3": "Ventral mesogastrium", "option4": "Falciform ligament", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mesogastrium_derivatives.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"606\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which is a ventral branch of the abdominal aorta? ", "option1": "Inferior phrenic artery", "option2": "Median sacral artery", "option3": "Superior mesenteric artery", "option4": "Gonadal artery", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Abdominal_aorta_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"607\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which is not a tributary of the inferior vena cava? ", "option1": "Left ovarian vein ", "option2": "Common iliac vein ", "option3": "Left phrenic vein ", "option4": "Hepatic vein", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IVC_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1313\" height=\"745\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) All of these organs are supplied by branches of the superior mesenteric artery, except-", "option1": "Vermiform appendix ", "option2": "Jejunum", "option3": "Sigmoid colon", "option4": "Ascending colon", "answer": "3", "exp": "Superior mesenteric artery supplies the <em><strong>midgut structures i.e. from second part of the duodenum up to the right two-third of the transverse colon.</strong></em> It also supplies part of te pancreatic head, by its first branch, the inferior pancreaticoduodenal artery.&nbsp;<br /><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Superior_mesenteric_artery_LMCQ_4BC0vRM.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"832\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) The portal vein is formed by union of the-", "option1": "Superior & inferior mesenteric veins", "option2": "Superior mesenteric & splenic vein", "option3": "Inferior mesenteric & splenic vein ", "option4": "Superior mesenteric and hepatic veins", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/portal_vein_mhs.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"598\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) The para-aortic group of lymph nodes drain-", "option1": "Abdominal part of GIT", "option2": "Kidneys", "option3": "Liver ", "option4": "Splenn", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/lymphatic_drainage_of_abdomen.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"648\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) The vagus supplies secretomotor fibres to the-", "option1": "Urinary bladder ", "option2": "Ileum ", "option3": "Anal canal ", "option4": "Descending colon", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Nerve_supply_of_abdomen.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"554\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) The narrowest part of the esophagus lies at the level of-", "option1": "Crossing with arch of aorta", "option2": "Crossing with left pulmonary bronchus", "option3": "Esophageal opening of the diaphragm", "option4": "Pharyngoesophageal junction", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Esophagus_constriction.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"371\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which does not form the stomach bed? ", "option1": "Splenic artery", "option2": "Transverse colon", "option3": "Body of pancreas ", "option4": "Diaphragm", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/stomach_bed_DteV3zh.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"607\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which is the artery of bleeding in duodenal ulcer? ", "option1": "Superior pancreaticoduodenal artery", "option2": "Inferior pancreagicoduodenal artery", "option3": "Gastroduodenl artery", "option4": "Superior mesenteric artery", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southea